        "question": "What does a credit repair VA usually do day to day?",
        "answer": "When status follow-up moves from the manager to the VA, day-to-day work should come from a defined queue rather than random requests. For this credit repair VA role, that may include client onboarding administration, CRM updates, document collection, and status follow-up. When recurring credit repair work includes appointment scheduling, the VA should know where new work appears, what a finished item looks like, and which exceptions need a manager. For teams delegating template organization, the exact daily mix depends on your business, so use the role title as a starting point, not as the complete scope."
