        "question": "Can a credit repair VA work independently?",
        "answer": "Yes, within a defined scope. Independence in a credit repair role should grow after the person has shown consistent accuracy and good judgment. Give the VA clear rules for routine client onboarding administration decisions and a short list of situations that require approval. The goal is not zero communication. The goal is for the VA to run routine credit repair work without repeated prompting and bring you exceptions with enough context to make a quick decision."
